{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/931956-ideas-for-self-possession","id":931956,"title":"Ideas for self possession?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-15T06:22:35-07:00","id":931956,"title":"Ideas for self possession?","content":"Need some ideas for self possession. The PC is a spirit/mind mage experimenting with summoning Astral (and sometimes ephemeral) entities, mainly within himself. He has taken Taoism tradition and is using something like cards filled with appropriate image, seals and runes as specialized tools (modified Taoist spirit amulets). Basically like summoning cards.<br /> <br /> So, which Astral entities (from any region) would you recommend for summoning/possession? For an example, Major Arcana would make a potent if dangerous pick, As well as Zodiac and maybe Ars Goetia demons?<br /> <br /> He also thinks of creating a personal Legacy oriented on the these techniques, Any recommendations or ideas?.<br /> <br /> Edit: can the mage act in astral and real world at the same time?<br /> what about an Astral sorcerer splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 07-15-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T03:27:17-07:00","id":936995,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:gotham\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, the potential pop references here is over 9000</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/931956-ideas-for-self-possession#post931956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has taken</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/931956-ideas-for-self-possession#post931956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Taoism tradition</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and is </span></span><b>using something like cards</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> filled with appropriate image, </span></span><b>seals and runes </b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as specialized tools (modified Taoist spirit amulets). Basically like summoning cards.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This sounds to me like the </span></span><b>Avatar </b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(from Avatar: The Last Airbender, full with taoism philosophy) learned how to </span></span><b>seal entities into cards</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (similar with the Pharaohs in Yu-Gi-Oh!!!) and is trying to accomplish it with a </span></span><b>runic alchemical circle</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (from Full Metal Alchemist)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Some backstory filtered by MtAw fluff</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-Avatar Wan was a mortal human that in order to </span></span><b>bring balance</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to his unknown world, mastered all &quot;arcana&quot; by merging himself with Raava, the embodiment of harmony, as mortals were unable to master all arcana, Together they sealed Vaatu, the embodiment of Chaos, in a multi-arcana prison. After merging with Raava, he was granted it's ability to reincarnate. Thus he became the first Avatar, master of all &quot;elements&quot;.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-The 18th Dynasty of Egypt faced an increasing spiritual mayhem as spirits of all kinds materialised and caused havoc in the area. In order to stop this madness, the old priests created through forbiden magic the Millenium Items; seven artifacts that could </span></span><b>force the monsters inside material items</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> like stones and cards.</span></span></span></span><br /> -Magic has rules. These rules the people of Amestris (unknown world) know well, or at least they think they do. The practice is simple enough for those with the talent though. A magic circle must be drawn,<b> inscribed with runes and symbols</b>. The rule is that magic requires balance; In order to gain something you need to sacrifice something of equal &quot;value&quot; in return. But who decides that value and what is its currency?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T04:59:25-07:00","id":937007,"title":"","content":"#CardCaptorSakura ?<br /> <br /> What role do you plan on this taking in the campaign? Do you plan on it being a simple buff or do you plan to play up the horror or the diplomacy or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T08:50:48-07:00","id":937111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/931956-ideas-for-self-possession?p=937007#post937007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#CardCaptorSakura ?<br /> <br /> What role do you plan on this taking in the campaign? Do you plan on it being a simple buff or do you plan to play up the horror or the diplomacy or what?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> horror is always present in CoD. But this strategy is good exactly because it is very versatile, you can be diplomat/warrior/crafter and of course the process of acquiring the cards is an adventure in and itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:35:32-07:00","id":937222,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a variant Clavicularius that uses cards as physical representations of keys, to me.<br /> <br /> 1e let you use Multitasking to act in both sides of the Astral Barrier or the Dreamspeaker's first attainment.<br /> Not far enow into 2e to say anything definitive, just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T00:16:33-07:00","id":937501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/931956-ideas-for-self-possession?p=937222#post937222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a variant Clavicularius that uses cards as physical representations of keys, to me.<br /> <br /> 1e let you use Multitasking to act in both sides of the Astral Barrier or the Dreamspeaker's first attainment.<br /> Not far enow into 2e to say anything definitive, just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeap. you can do that too if you prefer using Goetia demons. each card would even give +1 die bonus for yantra and +1-2 duration for runes. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}